===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|aviation}} A [[mechanism]] that [[secure]]s an [[aircraft]]'s [[landing gear]] in the [[retract]]ed [[position]], helping to [[prevent]] an [[uncommanded]] gear [[deployment]] during [[flight]].
#* {{quote-book|en|date=29 March 1986|author=w:National Transportation Safety Board|title=Aircraft Accident Report: China Airlines Boeing 747-SP, N4522V, 300 Nautical Miles Northwest of San Francisco, California, February 19, 1985|chapter=1.12 Wreckage and Impact Information|url=https://www.ntsb.gov/investigations/AccidentReports/Reports/AAR8603.pdf|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220710162138/https://www.ntsb.gov/investigations/AccidentReports/Reports/AAR8603.pdf|archivedate=10 July 2022|accessdate=10 July 2022|pages=12–13|text=The left and right wing landing gear '''uplock''' assemblies had separated from their attachment points on the fuselage structure.  The interior skin and associated ribs on the left and right wing gear inboard doors were damaged in the vicinity of their striker plates and the striker plates also were damaged.  The doors were damaged in the area where the tires are located when the gears are retracted.</p><p>The left and right body landing gear '''uplock''' hooks were found in the locked-up position, but the fasteners of their '''uplock''' support bracket assemblies had failed at the attach points to the fuselage bulkhead.}}

